---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ClaimsBadges from '../components/ClaimsBadges.astro';
import BookBox from '../components/BookBox.astro';
---

<Layout title="Claims and rebates" description="Claim private health insurance through HICAPS on site. We also see patients through Medicare, DVA, TAC and WorkSafe.">
	<section class="page-hero">
		<div class="container">
			<h1>Claims &amp; Rebates</h1>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="container prose">
			<ClaimsBadges />

			<h2>Health Insurance Rebates</h2>
			<p>
				All patients covered by private health insurance at Bass Coast Podiatry can claim their treatment rebates through our electronic
				HICAPS facility on site. You will need to bring your private health insurance card with you in order to use this facility.
			</p>
			<p>See <a href="https://www.hicaps.com.au/" rel="noopener">www.hicaps.com.au</a></p>

			<h2>Medicare claims</h2>
			<p class="check">
				[CHECK WITH CLIENT] Medicare rules for allied health care plans changed on 1 July 2025 and the item numbers below may be out of
				date. The fee difference was last updated in November 2017. Please confirm the wording for this section.
			</p>
			<p>
				Patients may be eligible for Medicare rebated Podiatry care under the Enhanced Primary Care (EPC) program if their GP has provided
				the following MBS Chronic Disease Management services and forms:
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li>A GP Management Plan (GPMP), item 721 (or review item 732); AND</li>
				<li>Team Care Arrangements (TCAs), item 723 (or review item 732)</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				A Medicare rebate is available for a maximum of five (5) allied health services per patient each calendar year (January to
				December). The stated number of visits is a total number of visits between all allied health practitioners.
			</p>
			<p>
				If you have been referred by your General Practitioner through the Medicare Enhanced Primary Care (EPC) program, Bass Coast
				Podiatry will charge its normal consult fees and then electronically claim your rebate through Medicare to be credited to your
				account the same day. As of November 2017 the difference between our actual standard consult fee and the Medicare rebate is $9.05.
			</p>
			<p>See <a href="https://www.servicesaustralia.gov.au/medicare" rel="noopener">www.servicesaustralia.gov.au/medicare</a></p>

			<h2>Department of Veterans Affairs</h2>
			<p>
				Any patient referred to Bass Coast Podiatry through the Department of Veterans Affairs will need the appropriate referral (usually
				a D904 or written referral) from their General Practitioner.
			</p>
			<p>See <a href="https://www.dva.gov.au/" rel="noopener">www.dva.gov.au</a></p>

			<h2>TAC and WorkSafe</h2>
			<p>
				Bass Coast Podiatry will see patients referred by their general practitioner or specialist through TAC and WorkSafe. Please
				contact our administration team for referral eligibility or any questions regarding TAC or WorkSafe.
			</p>
			<p>See <a href="https://www.tac.vic.gov.au/" rel="noopener">www.tac.vic.gov.au</a></p>
			<p>See <a href="https://www.worksafe.vic.gov.au/" rel="noopener">www.worksafe.vic.gov.au</a></p>

			<div class="claims-book">
				<BookBox />
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>

<style>
	.claims-book {
		margin-top: var(--space-xl);
	}
</style>
